From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:53:42 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] BSS Load: Update the Beacon frame only when the element
 changes

Every bss_load_update_period the Beacon frame was rebuilt and handed to
the driver, whether or not the values the BSS Load and ESP elements are
built from had changed. With mac80211 each update also reapplies the BSS
parameters (CTS protection, preamble, AP isolation, ...), which a driver
with an offloading firmware turns into a burst of firmware commands and
a new Beacon template for every BSS every few seconds. On a quiet
channel two updates in three carried the same elements.

Remember what the current Beacon frame advertises (station count,
channel utilization and the radio's own share of it, which the ESP
element uses) and skip the update when none of them changed.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
---
 src/ap/beacon.c   | 5 +++++
 src/ap/bss_load.c | 8 +++++++-
 src/ap/hostapd.h  | 5 +++++
 3 files changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ap/beacon.c b/src/ap/beacon.c
index 2b6eabc..7152db6 100644
--- a/src/ap/beacon.c
+++ b/src/ap/beacon.c
@@ -2523,6 +2523,11 @@ int ieee802_11_build_ap_params(struct hostapd_data *hapd,
 
 	tailpos = hostapd_get_rsne(hapd, tailpos, tailend - tailpos);
 	tailpos = hostapd_eid_bss_load(hapd, tailpos, tailend - tailpos);
+	hapd->beacon_bss_load_set = true;
+	hapd->beacon_bss_load_num_sta = hapd->num_sta;
+	hapd->beacon_bss_load_chan_util = hapd->iface->channel_utilization;
+	hapd->beacon_bss_load_chan_util_tx =
+		hapd->iface->channel_utilization_tx;
 	tailpos = hostapd_eid_ap_channel_report(hapd, tailpos);
 	tailpos = hostapd_eid_rm_enabled_capab(hapd, tailpos,
 					       tailend - tailpos);
diff --git a/src/ap/bss_load.c b/src/ap/bss_load.c
index e9baafc..99eb864 100644
--- a/src/ap/bss_load.c
+++ b/src/ap/bss_load.c
@@ -55,7 +55,13 @@ static void update_channel_utilization(void *eloop_data, void *user_data)
 		return;
 	}
 
-	ieee802_11_set_beacon_per_bss_only(hapd);
+	/* A Beacon frame update reprograms the whole BSS in the driver; skip
+	 * it when the BSS Load and ESP elements would not change. */
+	if (!hapd->beacon_bss_load_set ||
+	    hapd->beacon_bss_load_num_sta != hapd->num_sta ||
+	    hapd->beacon_bss_load_chan_util != iface->channel_utilization ||
+	    hapd->beacon_bss_load_chan_util_tx != iface->channel_utilization_tx)
+		ieee802_11_set_beacon_per_bss_only(hapd);
 
 	if (get_bss_load_update_timeout(hapd, &sec, &usec) < 0)
 		return;
diff --git a/src/ap/hostapd.h b/src/ap/hostapd.h
index b5d6532..7e67ac7 100644
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.h
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.h
@@ -195,6 +195,11 @@ struct hostapd_data {
 	u8 own_addr[ETH_ALEN];
 
 	int num_sta; /* number of entries in sta_list */
+	/* The load the current Beacon frame advertises (BSS Load, ESP) */
+	bool beacon_bss_load_set;
+	int beacon_bss_load_num_sta;
+	u8 beacon_bss_load_chan_util;
+	u8 beacon_bss_load_chan_util_tx;
 	struct sta_info *sta_list; /* STA info list head */
 #define STA_HASH_SIZE 256
 #define STA_HASH(sta) (sta[5])
-- 
